.TH SDL_ReleaseCameraFrame 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ReleaseCameraFrame \- Release a frame of video acquired from a camera.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_camera.h>
.PP
.BI "void SDL_ReleaseCameraFrame(SDL_Camera *camera, SDL_Surface *frame);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Let the back-end reuse the internal buffer for camera\[char46]
.PP
This function _must_ be called only on surface objects returned by
.BR SDL_AcquireCameraFrame ()\[char46]
This function should be called as quickly as possible after acquisition, as SDL keeps a small FIFO queue of surfaces for video frames; if surfaces aren\(aqt released in a timely manner, SDL may drop upcoming video frames from the camera\[char46]
.PP
If the app needs to keep the surface for a significant time, they should make a copy of it and release the original\[char46]
.PP
The app should not use the surface again after calling this function; assume the surface is freed and the pointer is invalid\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I camera
opened camera device\[char46]
.TP
.I frame
the video frame surface to release\[char46]
.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_AcquireCameraFrame (3)
